        "title": "28 Top Secret Websites To Make Money This Year: Up to $7,000/mo",
        "link": "https://www.sidehustlenation.com/secret-websites-to-make-money/",
        "source": "Side Hustle Nation",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-18T19:44:08.472243+00:00",
        "image": "https://www.sidehustlenation.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/data-annotation.jpg",
        "full_content": "Tired of hearing about the same old ways to make money online?\nWe’ve all heard about Etsy, Fiverr, and eBay…\nBut, you know, there’s a whole world of other websites out there that can help you earn some extra cash.\nSome of these sites are real hidden gems, flying under the radar while offering some serious opportunities.\nOk, confession time — so they’re not really secret websites to make money.\nThey’re more like “secret” websites to make some extra money.\nLet’s jump in!\n1. User Interviews\nUser Interviews facilitate customer feedback interviews online and over the phone.\nI’ve earned $105 with User Interviews so far, in exchange for about an hour and a half. Check out our full User Interviews review for more.\nUser Interviews is a legit facilitator of online (and in-person) consumer research studies. Participants can get paid (generally $50-150/hr) to share their opinion and shape future products and services. While this won’t replace your day job, it can be a nice supplemental income.\n- One of the best-paying survey companies I've found.\n- Easy to sign-up.\n- Lots of new studies added every week.\n- Can be difficult to get selected.\n2. Arrived: Hands-Off Real Estate Investing\nReal estate investing is one of the oldest and most popular side hustles in the books … but houses are expensive!\nThankfully, new platforms like Arrived make it easy to invest in income-generating properties—with as little as $100.\nThe company pools money to buy rental properties, manages them, and then distributes the cash flow every month.\n- Earn quarterly dividends\n- Completely hands-off\n- Low minimum investment ($100)\n- Limited liquidity\n- Not super diversified\n- Listings can sell out quickly\n3. Unclaimed.org: Find Missing Money\nDid you know there is over $42 billion in unclaimed funds in the United States? This is according to the National Association of Unclaimed Property Administrators (NAUPA).\nSearch databases at sites like Unclaimed.org to see if you’re owed any unclaimed money.\nTotally random, but I found $35 in Nevada from an older company of mine!\n4. Rare Patient Voice\nPatients and caregivers can earn $120/hour while helping advance medical research.\nA leading source for medical research, Rare Patient Voice pays patients and caregivers $120 an hour.\nMost of the studies are phone or webcam interviews, and you can browse a full list of available studies on their site.\nIf you suffer from any sort of medical condition (even if it’s not super rare), I think this one is worth a look.\n5. Debbie: Get Paid to Save Money\nDebbie is a unique app that pays you to pay off your debt and build savings.\nAfter you create your new account, link your existing checking, credit card, or savings accounts so Debbie can track your spending and payments.\nDebbie has already paid over $2.3M in cash rewards to consumers, and most users can expect to earn over $50 per month in cash rewards.\nAs a bonus, they’ll even give you a $5 reward to get started.\nHow does Debbie make money? Debbie‘s partner banks and credit unions pay them for referring new users, and they pass a portion of that revenue on to you.\n6. Data Annotation\nIf you’re willing to put in some serious hours, DataAnnotation offers pay ranging from $25-$100 per hour.\nThis involves training AI systems in various ways like editing, content flagging, grammar checks, and more.\nIt’s admittedly grueling work, but can be a good way to make money online for beginners.\nAdditional similar sites in this space include Outlier and TaskVerse.\n7. Prolific\nAnother lesser-known site to make money is Prolific, which specializes in “world changing” academic research.\nStudies range from quick 5-10 minute surveys to more in-depth questionnaires taking around 30 minutes.\nTheir academic nature makes hourly rates higher than many online survey sites.\nJackie Mitchell reported earning $10–$30 a day on Prolific when there were open studies matching her demographics. The sign-up process involves a waitlist, however, as researchers want balanced pools of participants.\nCheck out our full Prolific review to learn more.\n8. Honeygain: Get Paid for Your Internet Bandwidth\nHoneygain lets you earn passive income just by sharing your unused internet bandwidth.\nAll you have to do is install the app, and it runs in the background while you go about your day.\nHoneygain uses your internet to gather web statistics, and you get paid for it.\nIt’s passive income at its easiest, though you won’t get rich from it.\nStill, if you have internet to spare, why not make a few bucks?\nPro Tip: You can run Honeygain on multiple devices for more earnings.\n9. Wynter\nWynter is a newer market research company that pays up to $600 an hour for your opinion.\nThey focus on B2B studies targeting industry professionals, and list clients like:\n- Shopify\n- Hubspot\n- Intercom\n- and more\nStudies are invite-only, so make sure to fill in as many of your professional details as you can when you create your profile.\nI made $15 on my first 15-minute test.\n10. Mediaprobe\nIn researching ways to get paid to watch videos, I came across Mediaprobe.\nThe market research panel pays for your biometric responses to certain TV shows — to see how audiences really feel about what they’re watching.\nMediaprobe typically pays around $5 per hour of watch time, which is a cool way to get paid for an activity you might already be doing!\n11. Cambly – Get Paid to Chat in English\nCambly is a hidden gem for native or fluent English speakers.\nThis site pays you to chat with students from around the world who are learning English.\nNo teaching experience is necessary, making it perfect for anyone looking to make money while chatting casually.\nHow to get started: Sign up on Cambly, set up your tutor profile, and start chatting with students online.\nHow much you can make: Cambly pays around $10 to $12 per hour.\nChatting for a few hours each day could easily add up to an extra $200 or more per week.\nPro Tip: Focus on building rapport with students so they request you for future sessions, securing a consistent flow of income.\nIf you have a skill you can teach others, Skillshare allows you to create and sell your own video courses.\nFrom graphic design to photography, cooking, or coding, there’s always a demand for good courses.\nOnce you create and upload your course, students can enroll, and you’ll earn passive income each time someone takes it.\nPro Tip: Produce high-quality, engaging video content to attract more students and reviews.\n12. Test.IO: Get Paid to Test Websites and Apps\nIf you like finding bugs and enjoy testing websites or apps, Test.IO pays you to do just that.\nYou don’t need to be a tech expert; you simply sign up, start testing, and report bugs.\nThe more bugs you find, the more you get paid.\nEach test pays differently depending on the complexity, and some tests can be done in just a few minutes.\nPro Tip: Aim to be one of the first testers on new projects for better chances of finding critical bugs!\n13. Swappa: Cash for Your Old Tech\nGot an old phone, tablet, or gaming console gathering dust?\nSwappa makes it super easy to sell your used electronics and other gadgets. No haggling or meeting up with buyers required.\nHow it works:\n- Find your product in the Swappa catalog\n- Create a listing and upload photos\n- Get approved by the moderation team\n- Get paid when it sells!\nHow to make $500: If you’ve got a few old tech items lying around, selling them on Swappa can bring in some quick cash.\nBig-ticket items like smartphones or gaming consoles can get you close to your goal in one go.\n14. Lightster\nLightster is a unique money making app and website, where you get matched with brands and researchers based on your profile.\nTo get started, you’ll add some demographic information about yourself and answer some questions about your experience and interests.\nAfter that, you may see some questions pop up in the app. Answer those to qualify for paid research conversations that pay $1 per minute.\nI got invited to my first half hour session within a couple weeks of downloading the app, and got paid (via Amazon gift card) right away.\n15. Neighbor: Rent Out Your Storage Space\nIf you’ve got extra storage space, you can rent it out on Neighbor.com.\nWhether it’s a garage, basement, or even a closet, you can make money by storing other people’s belongings.\nIt’s like Airbnb for storage, and the best part is you don’t have to do much—just let people store their items and collect rent.\nPro Tip: Secure renters for longer-term storage agreements to create steady income without much hassle.\n16. PeoplePerHour: Freelancing for Short Gigs\nPeoplePerHour is a lesser-known but highly effective platform for freelancers.\nIt’s a great way to offer services like writing, graphic design, coding, and more. You can find short, quick gigs and get paid right away.\nHow to get started: Create a profile on PeoplePerHour, list your skills, and apply for posted gigs.\nJobs vary from long-term projects to one-off tasks that pay instantly.\nHow much you can make: Freelancers can earn anywhere from $20 to $200 per gig, depending on their skillset and job complexity.\nPro Tip: Focus on fast-delivery jobs to build your reputation and increase earnings quickly.\n17. Airtasker: Get Paid for Odd Jobs\nIf you’re good with your hands or don’t mind doing random tasks, Airtasker can be a great source of extra income.\nWhether it’s assembling IKEA furniture, running errands, or even helping someone move, there’s always someone looking for help.\nThe sign-up process is super easy.\nOnce you’re set up, you can choose which tasks to accept based on your availability and skills.\nPro Tip: Start by pricing your services competitively. As you build up reviews, you can increase your rates!\n18. Second to None: Mystery Shopping + Surveys\nSecond To None offers an exciting money-making opportunity through its mystery shopping program.\nAs a mystery shopper, you can earn extra income by evaluating customer experiences for leading brands across the U.S. and Canada.\nThis flexible gig allows you to choose assignments that fit your schedule, making it an ideal side hustle.\nHow to get started: Create a free shopper profile on the CX Group Shopper Hub.\nThe company values shoppers who enjoy interacting with people and can provide detailed feedback.\nPro Tip: To succeed, you’ll need:\n- strong observation skills\n- good time management\n- reliable transportation\n19. Dolly: Get Paid to Help with Moving and Deliveries\nDolly is a platform that connects people who need help moving, hauling, or delivering large items with “Helpers” who can provide that service.\nIf you have a truck, van, or even just the ability to lift and move heavy objects, Dolly could be a great way to make money on the side.\nHow to get started: Sign up on Dolly as a “Helper” or “Hand” (Helpers need a truck, while Hands assist with labor).\nOnce approved, you can start accepting jobs that fit your schedule.\nHow much you can make: Dolly Helpers can earn $30 to $50 per hour, while Hands typically make $15 to $25 per hour.\nA few large moving or delivery jobs can quickly help you reach $500 to $2,000 in a short time.\n20. Swimply: Rent Out Your Pool\nIf you have a backyard pool, Swimply is a fantastic platform that allows you to rent it out by the hour to people in your area who want to swim or host pool parties.\nThink of it as the Airbnb for pools!\nThis platform is perfect for pool owners who want to turn their underused outdoor space into a money-making opportunity.\nHow to get started: Sign up on Swimply, create a listing for your pool with high-quality photos, set your hourly rate, and availability.\nOnce your pool is listed, people in your area can book it for private use.\nHow much you can make: Depending on your location and the quality of your pool, you can charge anywhere from $40 to $100 per hour.\nHosting a few bookings each week could quickly add up to $500-$2,000 a month, especially during the summer months.\n21. WeGoLook: Get Paid to Inspect\nWeGoLook allows you to get paid for inspecting things like cars, real estate properties, or equipment.\nYou perform on-site inspections, take photos, and fill out reports for clients.\nThis platform is perfect if you’re detail-oriented and don’t mind doing a little legwork.\nPro Tip: Combine multiple “looks” in the same area to maximize your time and earnings!\n22. JustAnswer: Get Paid to Answer Questions\nSites like JustAnswer offer a flexible side hustle, where you can get paid to answer questions. JustAnswer experts earn an average of $2,000-$7,000 per month.\nOnce you apply as an expert, JustAnswer connects you with people who have questions. You can set your own hours and the types of questions you’re best-qualified to answer.\nYou’ll get paid for each customer you help, but the big advantage is that JustAnswer does all the marketing for you.\n23. HealthyWage: Get Paid to Lose Weight\nBet on yourself to hit your weight loss goal, and win an average of $1300 when you achieve it.\n- Get paid to build healthy habits\n- Set your own goals and timeline\n- You'll lose money if you don't hit your goal\n- Prize may not be motivating enough\nIf you’re looking to lose weight, you might want to check out HealthyWage. This cool service lets you put a friendly wager on your weight loss.\nIf you meet your goal, you can cash in — to the tune of $500 or more! (Here’s our full HealthyWage review.)\nIf you are looking to get healthy this year, why not make some money at the same time.\nClick here to see how much your prize might be.\n24. Hetal: Record Store Shelves\nWhile you’re running your errands, check for local gigs on Hetal.\nThese usually involve taking a video of a few aisles in a store, and pay $10-13.\n25. UserFeel: Website Testing\nIf you enjoy giving feedback on websites, UserFeel will pay you to test the usability of websites and apps.\nYou’ll be asked to perform simple tasks and share your thoughts on how user-friendly the experience was.\nEach test pays $3-30, and takes between 3 and 60 minutes.\nPro Tip: Provide detailed feedback to get higher ratings and receive more frequent testing opportunities.\n26. Society6: Turn Your Art into Income\nIf you’re an artist or designer, you need to know about Society6.\nThis platform allows you to upload your designs, and they handle the printing and shipping.\nYour art can be printed on anything from phone cases to wall art to shower curtains.\nEvery time someone buys a product with your design, you earn a commission.\nIt’s perfect if you’re creative and want to see your designs come to life without dealing with inventory or shipping.\nPro Tip: Promote your designs on social media to drive more traffic to your Society6 store.\nWe’ve been covering Sharetown for a while, but it is still a bit of a secret to most people.\nAs a part-time Sharetown rep, you’ll pick up gently-used furniture and mattress returns from direct-to-consumer brands.\nSince the items aren’t new, the companies can’t really take them back and resell them — but you can. The Sharetown reps I’ve connected with report earning $150-250 per item.\nAnd the cool part is the inventory doesn’t cost you anything until it sells.\nCheck out our full Sharetown review to learn more.\nSharetown reps make money by reselling gently-used furniture and bed-in-a-box mattresses. Top reps earn $4000+ per month.\n- Low startup costs\n- Great earning power\n- No hunting for inventory\n- Requires a truck or SUV\n- Bulky items to store\n- Not available in all areas\n28. Cashwalk: Get Paid to Walk\nCashwalk pays you to track your steps, with power users earning $5 every 6-8 weeks, or around $30 a year. (Available in the US only.)\nCheck out our full Cashwalk review to learn more.\nThe Secret’s Out: Lots of Unique Websites to Make Money\nThat’s our list of lesser-known websites that can help you earn some extra cash!\nWhether you’re walking dogs, flipping websites, or getting paid for your internet, there’s something here for everyone.\nThe best part? Most of these don’t require a huge time commitment, and you can start earning with a little effort.\nSo, what are you waiting for? Check out these sites, and start boosting your income today!\nSerious About Making More Money?\n- Start Your Free $500 Challenge. My free 5-day email course shows you how to add $500 to your bottom line.\n- Join the free Side Hustle Nation Community. The free Facebook group is the best place to connect with other side hustlers and get your questions answered.\n- Download The Side Hustle Show. My free podcast shares how to make extra money with actionable weekly episodes.",
