        "title": "AAP's Satyendar Jain arrested in alleged Jal Board corruption case",
        "link": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/india/aaps-satyendar-jain-arrested-by-delhi-acb-in-alleged-jal-board-corruption-case/articleshow/133326649.cms",
        "source": "India-News-Economic Times",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-18T19:44:08.471739+00:00",
        "image": "https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-133326671,width-1200,height-630,imgsize-67414,overlay-economictimes/articleshow.jpg",
        "full_content": "Listen to this article in summarized format\nThe ACB has arrested six accused persons in the case, including Jain, who served as the former Minister of Water in the Government of the National Capital Territory of Delhi.\nAlso read: Delhi Jal Board 'scam': ED files chargesheet against ex-Delhi Minister Satyendar Jain, 13 others\nThe other accused arrested are Udit Prakash Rai, an IAS officer and former CEO of the Delhi Jal Board; Ankit Srivastava, a former contractual consultant with the DJB; Nagendra Yadav, proprietor of M/s AN Enterprises; Raja Kumar Kurra, owner of M/s Euroteck Environement Pvt. Ltd; and Pankaj Verma, proprietor of M/s Srijanhar.\nAccording to the official, the arrests relate to alleged corruption in the Delhi Jal Board during the previous government.\nThe ACB is a law enforcement agency of the Government of the National Capital Territory of Delhi that investigates corruption-related allegations involving public servants and others.\nWhat is the Delhi Jal Board corruption case?\nThe case stems from alleged irregularities in the award of four tenders for the augmentation and upgradation of 10 Sewage Treatment Plants (STPs) operated by the Delhi Jal Board. The projects covered STPs at Pappankalan and Nilothi under Package 1, Najafgarh and Keshopur under Package 2, Coronation Pillar, Narela and Rohini under Package 3, and Kondli under Package 4.\nThe Enforcement Directorate had said its money-laundering investigation was based on an FIR registered by the Delhi government's Anti-Corruption Branch against Euroteck Environmental Pvt Ltd (EEPL) and others. The agency alleged that the tender conditions were manipulated to restrict the technology requirement to “IFAS technology with fixed media”, enabling EEPL to emerge as the sole technology supplier.\nAccording to ED, EEPL Managing Director Rajakumar Kurra and his associates allegedly paid Rs 6.73 crore in illegal commission and bribes through banking transactions and cash. The agency alleged that bogus invoices and advances were used to disguise some of the payments, while cash was routed through hawala channels.\nAlso read: ED provisionally attaches Rs 7.44 cr assets belonging to Satyendar Jain\nED had further alleged that the arrangement resulted in an undue profit of Rs 9.96 crore for EEPL. It said the total proceeds of crime linked to the alleged money-laundering offence amounted to Rs 17.70 crore.\nIn December 2025, the probe agency filed a prosecution complaint under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act against Jain, former DJB CEO Udit Prakash Rai, former DJB member Ajay, then Chief Engineer Satish Chandra Vashishth, and several private individuals and entities. The agency also said it had attached movable and immovable properties worth Rs 15.36 crore belonging to various persons in connection with the case.",
        "content": "Listen to this article in summarized format\nThe ACB has arrested six accused persons in the case, including Jain, who served as the former Minister of Water in the Government of the National Capital Territory of Delhi.\nAlso read: Delhi Jal Board 'scam': ED files chargesheet against ex-Delhi Minister Satyendar Jain, 13 others\nThe other accused arrested are Udit Prakash Rai, an IAS officer and forme...",
