        "full_content": "August the 16th, 2026 – Entrepreneur Mate Rimac has stated that some of the top Croatian export products are now luxury cars and battery systems.\nMate Rimac published on Facebook a table of the 50 largest Croatian goods exporters in 2025, compiled by the portal Lider. Index reports that among the top ten are two companies from Rimac’s business system. Bugatti Rimac took fourth place, and Rimac Technology seventh.\n“Croatia’s top export products in 2025 are oil and derivatives, medicines, transformers, luxury cars and their components, dietary supplements, battery and propulsion systems for cars, aluminium foil, food, HVAC systems and pharmaceutical products,” Rimac wrote. This is Rimac’s summary compiled on the basis of the activities of the companies at the top of Lider’s ranking. The table itself ranks companies according to the value of their exports.\nWho is actually on the table?\nIn first place is INA, which achieved 1.23 billion euros in exports in 2025. It is followed by Pliva Hrvatska with 474.4 million euros and Končar – Distribution and Special Transformers with 409.8 million euros.\nBugatti Rimac took fourth place with exports worth 369.1 million euros, which accounts for 94.33 percent of the company’s total revenues. In fifth place is Končar – Power Transformers with 313.5 million euros in exports, and sixth is dietary supplement manufacturer EMPWR with 227.4 million euros. Rimac Technology is in seventh place with exports worth 214 million euros, or an export share of 79.86 percent of total revenues. Also among the top ten are Aluflexpack Novi, Podravka and Klimaoprema.\nAccording to Lider’s data, the 50 largest Croatian goods exporters in 2025 achieved a total of 7.4 billion euros in exports. At the same time, Croatian goods exports exceeded 25 billion euros, of which 21.7 billion was generated by the manufacturing industry.",
