        "image": "https://millennialmoney.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/truist-logo-purple.jpg",
        "full_content": "If you’re looking at opening a new bank account or getting a new credit card, bank bonuses and promotions can help you land some free money in the process.\nMany banks, such as Truist Bank, offer seasonal and ongoing bonuses and offers, covering both personal as well as business consumers.\nI have personally held Truist consumer bank accounts in the past and have completed some of the bonuses listed below.\nTruist tends to offer bonuses on both their consumer and business products and are rather generous with the amounts as they look to grow their deposit base since merging SunTrust and BB&T to form Truist.\nCurrent Truist Bank Bonuses\nHere is the list of the current Truist promotions and bonuses that you can take advantage of today:\n- Truist One Checking: $400 Bonus\n- Truist Small Business Checking: $400 Bonus\n- Truist Enjoy Travel credit card: 20,000 Bonus Miles\nTruist One Checking: $400 Bonus\nTruist is offering a lucrative $400 bonus for new accountholders that open a Truist One Checking personal checking account.\nTaking advantage of this offer is easy.\nRequirements:\n- Open a Truist One Checking consumer checking account using promo code DC400TR1Q226 online or in a branch between March 26, 2026 and July 9, 2026\n- Make at least 2 qualifying direct deposits totaling at least $2,000 within 120 days of account opening\n- Complete at least 20 qualifying debit card purchases within 120 days of account openings\nThe qualifying checking account must be opened online and have a mailing address in: AL, AR, FL, GA, IN, KY, MD, MS, NC, NJ, OH, PA, SC, TN, TX, VA, WV or DC\nContinue Reading:\nTruist Small Business Checking: $400 Bonus\nTruist is offering a lucrative $400 bonus for accountholders that open a Truist Simple Business Checking or Dynamic Business Checking account.\nMany business checking accounts require a lot of cash to earn the bonus; however, Truist only requires a relative small deposit on hand.\nRequirements:\n- Open a new Simple Business Checking or Dynamic Business Checking account using promo code SB26Q2CHECKING online or in a branch between April 7, 2026, and July 9, 2026\n- Within 30 days, deposit at least $2,000.\nYou must be a new Truist business checking client.\nThe business’s physical address must be in: AL, AR, FL, GA, IN, KY, MD, MS, NC, NJ, OH, PA, SC, TN, TX, VA, WV or DC\nTruist Enjoy Travel credit card: 20,000 Bonus Miles\nThe Truist Enjoy Travel credit card is actually a pretty good card.\nIt rivals some of the larger American Express and Chase powerhouses in terms of the perks and earning potential, but comes with NO ANNUAL FEE.\nNot only can you get rewards faster than with other cards, but there’s also an ongoing promotion that can see you get as many as 20,000 bonus miles.\nThese points have a cash redemption value of $200.\nRequirements:\n- Apply for and get the Truist Enjoy Travel credit card\n- Make $1,500 worth of purchases within the first three months of opening the account\nHere’s a look at the current rewards earning structure:\n- Earn 2x miles per $1 spent on airfare, car rentals, and hotels.\n- Earn 1x miles per $1 spent on all other eligible purchases.\n- Plus, a statement credit up to $85 for TSA PreCheck® or Global Entry® fee is awarded once every four years.\nYou’ll also earn a 10% – 50% Loyalty Travel Bonus based on your Truist deposit relationship when you redeem your rewards for travel through the rewards program.\nThere is more good news as any points you earn also do not expire for as long as the account remains open.\nFAQs\nWhat are bank bonuses?\nBank bonuses are cash rewards and other perks the bank gives to its customers for meeting specific criteria.\nIn most cases, these involve depositing a certain amount of new money into a new account and holding it there for some time.\nThere are several reasons why a bank does this. These reasons can include anything from attracting new customers to rewarding customers that have been with the bank for a very long time.\nEither way, taking advantage of these bonuses on offer can see you get extra cash, which is always welcome.\nWhat should I look out for?\nWhile free money is always something to look forward to, it’s important to take note of the fine print that accompanies any sign-up bonus you’re thinking of taking.\nMost promotions and bonuses require several direct deposits to be made into the account within so many days of opening the account (has to be a deposit by your employer or an outside agency).\nThe funds usually have to be kept in the deposit account for several months before you become eligible for the bonus.\nSome offers are available online, while others are exclusively in-branch.\nDo keep in mind that some accounts also have a fee that has to be paid every fee period, which is mostly set to monthly.\nThe applicable APR rate is another important point to take into consideration, especially the applicable rate once any introductory offers are over.\nUltimately, each promotion is subject to its own terms and conditions.\nThis makes it important to make sure you understand the restrictions and obligations surrounding each offer you want to take up.\nAll information should be available through the promotion page on the bank’s website. If you cannot find it, be sure to ask one of the bank’s representatives for a copy.\nWe will now look at the different bonuses on offer, how you can take advantage of them, and what other perks you can look forward to when opening a new Truist consumer account or business account.\nIs A Truist Bank Bonus For You?\nTruist is an excellent bank if you’re looking to open a new account while making your money go further by taking advantage of some bonus offer codes.\nAs with most bank bonuses, these are only available to new Truist customers.\nSo, for example, if you’re a current owner of a Truist consumer account, it is best to check with a customer service rep before applying for a new card or account so that you can be sure that you’ll definitely get the bonus.\nBefore opening a new bank account to claim any bonus, be sure to take the time to shop around.\nMany card issuers are offering bonuses right now, but looking at the bonus requirements and eligibility criteria set by the bank can help you narrow it down to the ones that could really work for you.\nTake the time to understand the eligibility requirements to avoid disappointment.\nSome accounts also have a monthly service fee, but in most cases, this can be waived by meeting specific requirements.\nMany banks around the country have ongoing and seasonal promotions, but you do have to be mindful of their expiration dates as they change frequently.",
