        "full_content": "Over 1,800 Afghan Returnees Cross Routes in Single Day\nA total of 1,843 Afghan migrants representing 229 families returned to the country on Sunday via the Torkham, Spin Boldak, Pul-e-Abrisham, and Islam Qala crossing routes. on arrival, they underwent registration and verification procedures before receiving essential support services.\nHamidullah Fitrat, Deputy Spokesman for the Islamic Emirate, stated in a release that, according to the daily report from the Secretariat of the High Commission for Refugees, 728 individuals from 141 families entered through Torkham. Meanwhile, 23 people from three families returned via Spin Boldak, 272 individuals from 74 families through Pul-e-Abrisham, and 42 people from 11 families via Islam Qala.\nFollowing their entry, relevant committees carried out registration, verification, reception, transportation, financial aid, healthcare, and public awareness activities.\nAs part of these efforts, 1,286 individuals from 241 families were transported to Nangarhar, Kunar, Laghman, Kabul, and several other provinces.\nTransportation costs amounted to 817,290 AFN for returnees from Torkham, 2,200 AFN from Spin Boldak, and 99,000 AFN from Kabul.\nIn addition, financial assistance totaling 2,002,000 AFN was distributed to 252 families. Some returnees received medical examinations and treatment, while food and telecommunication services were made available at designated centers.\nA total of 145 registered SIM cards with active packages were also distributed to the returnees.\nAuthorities provided returnees with guidance on registration procedures, transport options, financial aid, temporary shelter, and other essential services.",
