    {
        "title": "iHeartMedia Spotlights New Music from Beyoncé and Ariana Grande; Names STELLA LEFTY and FLO as Latest ‘On The Verge’ Artists",
        "link": "https://content.iheartmedia.com/press/iheartmedia-spotlights-new-music-beyonce-and-ariana-grande-names-stella-lefty-and-flo-latest",
        "source": "iHeartMedia",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-18T19:44:08.470283+00:00",
        "image": null,
        "full_content": "NEW YORK – July 31, 2026 – iHeartMedia highlighted new music and artists alike recently with special programming.\nOn Friday, Beyoncé’s new single “MORNING DEW (DONK)” was featured as an iHeartRadio Spotlight across all iHeartRadio R&B stations while several songs from Ariana Grande’s new album “petal” were featured in New Music Friday slots across all iHeartRadio CHR stations.\nThis summer, iHeartMedia named STELLA LEFTY and FLO as the latest ‘On The Verge’ artists, with singer-songwriter STELLA LEFTY featured across iHeartCountry stations with her single “Boston” and hit British girl group FLO featured across iHeartRadio Rhythm CHR stations with their single “Don’t Break Her Heart.” iHeartMedia’s ‘On The Verge’ program helps build awareness for up-and-coming artists through its radio airplay and historically, all ‘On The Verge’ artists have charted in the top 30, with more than half landing in the top 10 and over a third claiming the No. 1 chart slot.\nFor the latest news, music fans can download the iHeartRadio app; follow iHeartRadio on Instagram, TikTok, Twitter/X, Facebook and YouTube; and visit iHeartRadio.com.",
