        "full_content": "Lisa Rinna and Her Therapist Are Convinced Patrick Clancy Murdered His Kids\nFormer Real Housewives of Beverly Hills star Lisa Rinna says she and her therapist are convinced Patrick Clancy, not Lindsay Clancy, murdered his three children.\nIn a video she posted to TikTok, Rinna says “Alright he did it. Patrick did it. Patrick’s the one who did it. Not Lindsay. Patrick did it.”\nShe goes son to say she discussed the case with her therapist and her therapist looked at her and said, “He did it.” Rinna then says she agreed with her therapist’s assessment.\nLindsay Clancy is currently on trial for killing her three children at her Duxbury, Massachusetts home in January 2023. Afterwards she attempted to take her own life by jumping from a second-story window, leaving her paralyzed.\nLindsay Clancy has admitted to killing the children, but her defense argues that she was suffering from severe postpartum mental illness, including postpartum psychosis. Her defense also argues that her psychiatric treatment and medications contributed to her deterioration.\nProsecutors, meanwhile, contend that the killings were deliberate and that Clancy understood what she was doing.\nRinna reasons that the children were strangled and that’s not what a woman would do. However, according to the FBI, women are actually more likely to strangle than men are, though the actual number of women strangling victims is lower overall because men commit the vast majority of violent crime.\nOnline commenters have found Patrick Clancy’s behavior ranges from negligent (leaving Lindsay alone with the children after she told him she was frightened by her thoughts of harming them) to suspicious (leaving happy reviews for a hike just three weeks after his children’s funerals, quickly publicly forgiving Lindsay for the murders, quickly moving on to a new marriage).\nHowever, even Lindsay’s defense team isn’t alleging that Patrick did it. Lindsay confessed. Her defense is that she was in post-partum psychosis at the time, not that she is innocent.\nThank you for reading. Catch all of Thought Catalog’s latest on Facebook and our website.",
