        "full_content": "Salma Hayek Is a Grandma at 59, and She’s Calling the Baby “Panchito.”\nThe baby’s name is actually François, the fourth living generation to carry it. Salma decided he’s a “Panchito” instead, and she says he already loves it.\nThe baby boy is the fourth living François in the family, but Salma Hayek has other plans for what to call him.\n“We are blessed to welcome the fourth living generation of Francois’. Although I will call him Panchito. He seems to love it, and I cannot love him more,” she wrote on Instagram, alongside a video of her holding him and cooing to him in Spanish.\nHayek, 59, became a grandmother when her stepson François Pinault Jr., 38, welcomed his first child with his wife, Lara Cosima Henckel von Donnersmarck. She’s been part of the blended family since marrying François-Henri Pinault in 2009, and the couple share 18-year-old daughter Valentina.\n“My husband (the world’s coolest françois) and our son (the world’s cutest françois) … our first month as parents,” Henckel von Donnersmarck captioned a post of her own.\nThanks for spending time with Thought Catalog. Connect with us on Facebook and browse the rest of our website.",
