        "title": "A Mother and Son Spent 5 Years Hand-Making a Chinese Cartoon So Rough That Audiences Call It Proof No AI Touched It. It’s Now Grossed S$3.2 Million",
        "link": "https://thoughtcatalog.com/nadia-santiago/2026/08/a-mother-and-son-spent-5-years-hand-making-a-chinese-cartoon-so-rough-that-audiences-call-it-proof-no-ai-touched-it-its-now-grossed-s3-2-million/",
        "source": "Thought Catalog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-18T20:19:42.484955+00:00",
        "image": "https://thoughtcatalog.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-mother-and-son-spent-5-years-hand-making-a-chinese-cartoon-so-rough-that-audie.jpg?w=1200&h=630&crop=1",
        "full_content": "A Mother and Son Spent 5 Years Hand-Making a Chinese Cartoon So Rough That Audiences Call It Proof No AI Touched It. It’s Now Grossed S$3.2 Million\nXin Yumeng and his mother, Sun Lifang, taught themselves 3D modeling, animation, voice acting, and music to build “Niu Lai” almost entirely on second-hand gear.The animation is so stiff and low-budget that Chinese audiences started buying tickets just to laugh, and now its earnings almost match Spider-Man: Brand New Day.\nNiu Lai opened in 245 theaters on August 5 with no trailer, no interviews, and almost no one showing up. Its first 9 days brought in under US$1,200 total, with fewer than 300 tickets sold across the country.\nThen clips of the stiff, low-poly animation went viral on Weibo, and curious viewers flooded back in. By August 18 the film had grossed around S$3.2 million, with daily takings nearly on par with Spider-Man: Brand New Day, according to Chinese box-office platform Maoyan.\nDirector Xin Yumeng, an interior designer with no film training, built it over roughly 5 years with his mother, Sun Lifang. The two handled the writing, 3D modeling, animation, voice acting, and music between them. Sun even performed the ending theme.\nCritics called it “disaster-level” and “worse than AI-generated,” and audiences reportedly laughed all the way through screenings. Online, the mockery flipped into affection: viewers praised the crude, hand-crafted look as proof no AI was involved, and started comparing it to cult classic The Room.\n“You may regret for 80 minutes if you watch it, but if you don’t, you’ll regret it for life,” one widely shared post read, per the BBC. Xin has already announced a follow-up.\nWant more Thought Catalog? Follow us on Facebook or head to our website.",
        "content": "A Mother and Son Spent 5 Years Hand-Making a Chinese Cartoon So Rough That Audiences Call It Proof No AI Touched It. It’s Now Grossed S$3.2 Million\nXin Yumeng and his mother, Sun Lifang, taught themselves 3D modeling, animation, voice acting, and music to build “Niu Lai” almost entirely on second-hand gear.The animation is so stiff and low-budget that Chinese audiences started buying tickets just ...",
