        "title": "Trump Brought Natalie Harp, the Aide Maggie Haberman Calls His “Binky” and “Comfort Blanket”, on His Getaway Plane, While Marco Rubio and Stephen Miller Were Left Behind on Air Force One",
        "link": "https://thoughtcatalog.com/nadia-santiago/2026/08/trump-brought-natalie-harp-the-aide-maggie-haberman-calls-trumps-binky-and-comfort-blanket-on-his-getaway-plane-while-marco-rubio-and-stephen-miller-were-left-behind-on-air-force-one/",
        "source": "Thought Catalog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-18T20:19:42.484951+00:00",
        "image": "https://thoughtcatalog.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/trump-brought-natalie-harp-the-aide-maggie-haberman-calls-trump-s-binky-and-comf.jpg?w=1536&h=768&crop=1",
        "full_content": "Trump Brought Natalie Harp, the Aide Maggie Haberman Calls His “Binky” and “Comfort Blanket”, on His Getaway Plane, While Marco Rubio and Stephen Miller Were Left Behind on Air Force One\nNatalie Harp, also known as “the human printer”, leaves Trump handwritten notes calling him “the alpha and the omega.” She once slept in a maid’s room, then a women’s locker room, just to stay close to him at Bedminster. When a threat forced him onto a secret plane, she was one of three people he brought.\nHarp, 34, is a former One America News host who became Trump’s near-constant shadow. Colleagues call her “the human printer” for lugging a laptop, portable printer, and battery pack everywhere he goes, printing flattering articles and handing him hard copies on demand, sometimes in a Lululemon bag. She’s been seen running on foot behind his golf cart to deliver printouts.\nShe’s left adoring handwritten notes in his personal spaces: “You are all that matters to me,” “You’re the alpha and the omega,” “What would I be without you?” To stay physically close at Bedminster, she reportedly slept in a maid’s room and later the women’s locker room after being denied normal lodging. Trump has told staff she’s “the only one who loves me as much as my wife and my kids” and that “she’ll never leave me.”\nMaggie Haberman has called her Trump’s “binky” and “comfort blanket”, a living security blanket for emotional reassurance more than a policy aide. Her estranged brother, Preston Harp, has publicly called the dynamic “very unhealthy” and likened her to “his fan club.”\nThe decoy episode in July drew a line under all of it. After a NATO summit in Ankara, intelligence flagged a credible Iranian threat, and Trump slipped out a side door of the legacy Boeing 747 into a raised catering truck that carried a tiny group to a smaller C-32A. Harp was in that group, alongside longtime aide Dan Scavino and valet Walt Nauta. Rubio, Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent, and Stephen Miller stayed on the 747 as it flew on under the Air Force One call sign as a decoy.\nThanks for spending time with Thought Catalog. Connect with us on Facebook and browse the rest of our website.",
