        "image": "https://thoughtcatalog.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/in-china-hacks-is-called-the-diva-and-the-strawberry-and-fans-built-a-whole-sims.jpg?w=1499&h=768&crop=1",
        "full_content": "In China, ‘Hacks’ Is Called ‘the Diva and the Strawberry,’ and Fans Built a Whole Sims World Where the Characters Live Together in a Treehouse\nFans in Taiwan have shipped Deborah and Ava since season 1 under the name “Avorah,” and one corner of the fandom built a whole Sims world where the two women live together in a treehouse. Jean Smart is aware of the long-distance fandom, having received fan mail from China, and her “son’s Mandarin Twitter”.\n“The Diva and the Strawberry” is how a huge Chinese-language fanbase knows the HBO series Hacks. In Taiwan the show runs under the title 天后與草莓 (Tiānhòu yǔ Cǎoméi), casting Jean Smart’s Las Vegas comedy legend Deborah Vance as the “diva” and Hannah Einbinder’s sharp young writer Ava Daniels as the “strawberry.”\nMainland China gets a different name entirely: 绝望写手, roughly “Desperate Ghostwriter.” Hong Kong went with 職業槍手, “Hired Gun.”\nThe fandom runs deep. Beyond the treehouse Sims world, there’s a flood of fan art built around Deborah and Ava, whose mentor-and-mentee bond fans have shipped as “Avorah” since season 1. The show fed it in season 5, when the two fake a romance to score a fancy jumpsuit, a scene Einbinder and Smart said was “so much fun” to film.\nHacks ran five seasons from 2021 to 2026 and won Smart multiple Emmys for the role. The strawberry, is likely an homage to Einbinder’s strawberry blonde hair, but has not officially been confirmed.\nWant more Thought Catalog? Follow us on Facebook or head to our website.",
