        "image": "https://images.nintendolife.com/69ba640bd367d/large.jpg",
        "full_content": "Diablo IV has been rumoured for the Switch 2 for some time now, but according to a new report from Dealabs, it could be launching as soon as next month.\nDealabs has a strong history of accurate reports, and it states that Diablo IV: Age of Hatred Collection – which contains the base game along with the Vessel of Hatred and Lord of Hatred expansions – will release on Switch 2 on 15th September 2026.\nPriced at €69.99 / $69.99 / £62.99, an official announcement could take place at Gamescom this month, with pre-orders set to begin from 12th September to coincide with BlizzCon 2026. A retail release is also rumoured, but unfortunately it sounds like this will be a code-in-a-box release.\nIf accurate, this means Diablo IV joins an incredibly busy month for the Switch 2, with the likes of Wo Long: Fallen Dynasty, Onimusha: Way of the Sword, Fire Emblem: Fortune's Weave, and LEGO Batman: Legacy of the Dark Knight all set to launch within weeks of one another.\nStill, we're keen to see Diablo IV on Switch 2. Our pals over at Push Square had great things to say in their review from 2023, awarding it a score of 9/10:\n\"Diablo 4 is the true successor to the bad old days of action RPGs and oozes quality in its frenetic combat and deep, engaging character development. It tells a complex, gritty narrative set in the darkly beautiful world of Sanctuary. Even better, it provides a solid foundation for years of Diablo content to come.\"",
