        "full_content": "“Scam Goddess,” comedy podcast in which Laci Mosley and friends feast on crazy stories about frauds past and present, is now coming at you in video.\n“Scam Goddess” has joined iHeartMedia and Will Ferrell’s Big Money Players comedy podcast network — and the show has expanded into video, with a new YouTube channel where fans can watch full-length episodes going forward.\nIn each episode, Mosley — the self-proclaimed Queen of Scam — covers the hottest scams on the streets today while also breaking down the wildest robberies, grifts and assorted capers through history. Mosley is joined on the podcast to mull over the malfeasance by guests who have included Conan O’Brien, Jameela Jamil, Miranda Cosgrove, Lamorne Morris, Ayo Edebiri, Gayle King, JB Smoove, Nicole Byer and Matt Rogers.\nPopular on Variety\nMosley launched the “Scam Goddess” podcast in 2019. She penned a bestselling book of the same name that was published in 2024 and expanded the franchise with a Hulu original series that premiered last year. Mosley also staged a “Scam Goddess” sold-out national live tour with Live Nation. Her TV acting credits include “A Black Lady Sketch Show,” “Going Dutch” and “iCarly.”\nThe first “Scam Goddess” video episode, “F.R.A.U.D. Is Dope the Jonathan Dupiton Con With Langston Kerman,” premieres today and features comedian and “My Momma Told Me” host Langston Kerman. He joins the show to break down AI ads, “beach ab” shots and the “shoddy merch” Jonathan Dupiton released for Dupiton’s podcast “Rich and Unemployed.”\n“Scam Goddess” is now available through Big Money Players, distributed by iHeartPodcasts via the iHeartRadio app and major podcast platforms. The first full-length video episode premieres Aug. 18 on YouTube. New episodes are released weekly on Tuesdays (and archive episodes are re-released each Friday).\nWatch first video episode of “Scam Goddess” on YouTube:\nListen to the latest episode of “Scam Goddess” on iHeart:",
