        "image": "https://images.ctfassets.net/lzny33ho1g45/5zCubE81LBa7pi7uq4kqr1/5702ca07f913dbb60cc84afd667731cc/Automation_inspiration__4_.jpg",
        "full_content": "I have sent probably four hundred emails in my life that just said some version of \"does 2pm Thursday work for you?\" Calendly exists so none of us has to do that anymore. Invitees see your real availability and pick a slot without the back and forth.\nThat solves the booking problem. It doesn't solve everything else that comes with a new meeting, like syncing it to your team's calendar or logging the invitee in your CRM. That's where a Zap—our word for Zapier's automated workflows—comes in. Connect Calendly to thousands of other apps, and the rest of the process runs itself. Here's how.\nZapier is the most connected AI orchestration platform—integrating with thousands of apps from partners like Google, Salesforce, and Microsoft. Use forms, data tables, and logic to build secure, automated, AI-powered systems for your business-critical workflows across your organization's technology stack. Learn more.\nTable of contents\nTo get started with a Zap template—what we call our pre-made workflows—just click on the button. It only takes a few minutes to set up. You can read more about setting up Zaps here.\nAutomatically track meetings\nIf you need to report on sales goals or performance to other teams, keeping an automatic record of your meetings can save you from frantically scrolling through your calendar when someone asks for an update.\nUse one of these Zap workflows to automatically add your Calendly meeting info to your spreadsheet tool. If you're working with leads, try the first Zap—it uses an AI by Zapier step to analyze responses before they get logged. AI could scan the responses for buying intent, urgency, lead qualification, sentiment, or whatever else you can dream up.\nAdd new Calendly invitees to Google Sheets with AI analysis\nCreate Google Sheets rows from new scheduled Calendly events\nAnd if you're using Calendly Notetaker, you can also easily keep track of meeting recaps in your team's favorite tools:\nAdd new Calendly meeting recaps to Google Sheets rows\nCreate Notion database pages for new Calendly meeting recaps\nCreate Confluence pages for new Calendly meeting recaps\nCreate Google Docs for new Calendly meeting recaps\nAutomatically send meeting notifications\nNotifying attendees about upcoming meetings, time changes, or no-shows is an administrative task that just begs for automation. You can use Zapier to help with fine-grained notification schedules, reminders, and alerts.\nUse these Zap workflows to let the team know about new meetings the moment they're created. You can even send yourself a text when somebody cancels a meeting, so you don't waste time getting mentally ready for something that isn't happening.\nPost Microsoft Teams messages with new Calendly invitees\nSend WhatsApp Notifications messages when Calendly invitees cancel their appointments\nAnd if you're using Calendly Notetaker, you can easily share recaps after your calls. With this Zap, you can automatically post new meeting recaps in your team channels, complete with an AI-generated summary and action items so your team can quickly follow up.\nSend Slack channel messages for new Calendly meeting recaps\nIf your day is spent in your inbox instead of team chat, an email reminder does the trick. It's also a great way to remind clients and meeting attendees outside your team that you have a call coming up.\nGot another no-show? Send them an email. You might, for example, want to send them a personalized offer to keep them interested or a chance to reschedule at a later date. These Zap workflows can do this for you—automatically.\nSend emails via Gmail for new scheduled Calendly events\nSend Microsoft Outlook emails for new invitee created events in Calendly\nCreate tasks from Calendly meetings\nA meeting is usually just a first step, especially for client intros and sales calls. Make sure you properly follow up after a call—whether that's remembering to send a thank you email or prepare a contract—by automatically creating a task in your project management software for Calendly invitees.\nThis can be especially helpful if you pass tasks across your team and want to make sure nothing falls through the cracks. Give one of these workflows a try so you never miss a to-do.\nAdd items in monday.com for new invitees created in Calendly\nCreate ClickUp tasks for new Calendly meeting recaps\nCreate Asana tasks for action items from new Calendly meeting recaps\nAdd Calendly bookings to your other calendars\nAdding Calendly events to your work calendar quickly and automatically helps eliminate double-booking, especially if work colleagues have access to your free/busy times.\nWhile Calendly has a built-in connection with some popular calendar apps, sometimes you may want events to show up in more than one place or on a calendar that isn't connected to your account.\nUse the Zap workflows below to connect Google Calendar or Outlook to Calendly. In addition to automatically populating the new event's title, start and end times, you can also specify a standard meeting location, include a personal conference dial-in or video meeting, and set an event's color, visibility, and reminder schedule.\nCreate Google Calendar events from new scheduled Calendly events\nCreate Microsoft Outlook events for new invitees created in Calendly\nSet up video conferencing for Calendly meetings\nBy now, we've probably all experienced that moment of panic when you miss the start of the meeting because you can't find the right video conferencing link. That short delay gets your meeting off on the wrong foot, leaving you frazzled and apologetic before you even say hello.\nAutomation ensures this never needs to happen again. Use these Zap workflows to automatically set up video conferencing for Calendly events.\nSend new Calendly invitees a Google Meet video link\nCreate Zoom meeting registrants for new Calendly invitees\nRegister new Calendly invitees as Zoom webinar registrants with ease\nAdd Calendly invitees to your CRM and email marketing funnels\nAn introductory meeting is often just the first step toward a sale. Making sure your client gets the right follow-up is an important next step.\nThese Zap workflows add invitees and contacts to your customer relationship management (CRM) tool, so you can track relationships as they develop. You can even add notes to each client in your CRM, so if they miss an event it's a good idea for your sales team to know about it—so they can follow up accordingly.\nCreate or update Hubspot contacts for new Calendly invitees\nAdd or update LeadConnector opportunities for new Calendly invitees\nAdd a no-show in Calendly as a note to a Pipedrive customer\nAnother way to ensure that you and your organization remain top-of-mind during the purchasing decision is to automatically add invitees to your email marketing newsletters. This way, even when you're not speaking to prospects directly, you can share value, show them compelling information, and gently convince them to convert. Just make sure they've opted in to receive these types of emails before you add them.\nCreate Kajabi form submissions for invitee scheduled events in Calendly\nAdd or update ActiveCampaign contacts for new Calendly invitees\nCreate Mailchimp subscribers from new Calendly invitees\nAdd tagged subscribers to ConverKit from new Calendly events\nCreate Flodesk subscribers from new Calendly appointments\nDo more in less time with Calendly and Zapier\nCalendly makes it easy to schedule meetings without resorting to long email conversations. But with a little imagination and Zapier's ability to connect Calendly with dozens of other productivity, sales, and marketing tools, you can automate the entire meeting workflow. Think about it—no more double-booking, no more missed starts, and no rush to follow up when the meeting ends. What will you do with all your free time?\nThis piece was originally published in August 2020, with previous contributions by Jack Beaudoin, Elena Alston, and Steph Spector. It was most recently updated in August 2026.",
