        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2026/08/pocket-money-5.png",
        "full_content": "Growing up comes with a lot of firsts. The first time you go out with friends. The first solo trip to the café. The first time you need to make a payment without asking someone else to do it for you.\nFor teenagers, being able to make their own payments is a small but meaningful step towards independence. But for parents and families, that independence also comes with an obvious question: how do you give them freedom while still having visibility and control?\nThat is where Paytm Pocket Money comes in.\nPaytm Pocket Money makes Paytm UPI payments accessible to teenagers without requiring them to have their own bank account. It gives them the freedom to make everyday mobile payments, while parents or trusted family members can stay in control.\nFreedom for them. Control for you.\nWith Paytm Pocket Money, family members can give teenagers controlled access to make UPI payments. They can set spending limits, track payments and spending in real time, and manage the access whenever needed.\nSo, your teenager gets the freedom to pay independently, while you get visibility into how much is being spent. Simple.\nWhether it is making a payment while out with friends or requesting pocket money when needed, Paytm Pocket Money makes the experience easy to manage through the app.\nAnd the best part? Control stays with the family member who enables the access. It can be managed or revoked anytime, giving families greater flexibility and peace of mind.\nNot just for teenagers\nDespite the name, Paytm Pocket Money is not limited to teens.\nFamilies can also use it to give controlled spending access to spouses, elders, or other dependents who may need an easy way to make mobile payments without having their own bank account linked for this purpose.\nFor example, you may want to give an elderly family member access to make UPI payments while keeping an eye on spending. Or you may want to provide a dependent with a fixed spending limit for the month.\nPaytm Pocket Money helps make that possible through a simple family-led setup.\nA simple way to build responsible money habits\nIndependence is not just about having the freedom to spend. It is also about understanding how to manage money responsibly.\nWhen teenagers can make their own Paytm UPI payments within limits set by their family, they also begin to understand spending, budgeting, and financial responsibility.\nFamilies can see payments and spending in real time, while teenagers get the experience of managing their own everyday expenses.\nIt is a balance that works for both sides.\nPayments unki. Control aapka. Freedom dono ki.\nWith Paytm Pocket Money, families can make it easier for their loved ones to experience independent mobile payments, while still keeping the controls they need close at hand.\nBecause giving someone financial freedom does not mean giving up visibility.\nWith Paytm Pocket Money, both can go hand in hand.",
