        "full_content": "Amazon Quick now supports per-user resource limits\nAmazon Quick now enables administrators to set per-user limits on index storage and agent hours, giving them direct control over subscription costs. With limits management, administrators can create limit profiles that cap per-user consumption, helping prevent unexpected overage charges and ensuring subscription entitlements are used efficiently across their organization.\nFor example, an organization deploying Quick enterprise-wide to thousands of users can set account-level limit profiles to establish cost-predictable baselines, then assign higher limits to specific roles that require more agent hours. Administrators can create and assign limit profiles at the user, role, or account level, with a priority hierarchy that ensures the right users get the right capacity. When a user reaches their limit, new consumption is blocked while existing content is preserved.\nThis feature is available for Professional and Enterprise plans, in all AWS Regions where Amazon Quick agentic capabilities are supported. For more information, see the AWS Region table.\nLearn more about Amazon Quick by visiting the Quick website. To learn more about limit profiles, see Limits management in the Amazon Quick User Guide.",
